{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What criteria do you use to determine the success of your disaster recovery plans after an actual event has occurred?\nA: Kestrel Cloud assesses disaster recovery success through compliance with our internal DR standards and the timely execution of recovery protocols. Our compliance program, Kestrel Secure, mandates evaluations every quarter post-incident. Success is defined by meeting our RTO and RPO benchmarks, ensuring that our managed-container platform remains operational with minimal disruption. Customers are responsible for their data backups, while we handle infrastructure recovery."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure compliance with relevant regulations and standards in your business continuity and disaster recovery planning?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains compliance with our internal Kestrel Compliance Framework, which is aligned with NIST SP 800-34 and ISO 27031. Our business continuity and disaster recovery plans are reviewed quarterly to ensure they meet these standards. We rely on automated tools for backup and recovery processes, and customers are responsible for their own data redundancy strategies. Regular training sessions for our staff ensure everyone understands their roles in maintaining compliance."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the process for updating incident response plans based on findings from incident reviews, and who is responsible for approving these updates?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to our compliance program, which mandates annual reviews of incident response plans. Updates are based on findings from incident reviews, with the compliance officer approving changes. Customers are responsible for integrating their own incident response strategies with our framework."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you maintain awareness of emerging threats that could impact your business continuity, and what process do you follow to adapt your plans accordingly?\nA: Kestrel Cloud leverages its compliance program to stay informed about emerging threats. We conduct biannual reviews of our infrastructure against industry standards, including ISO 27001 and NIST. Our incident response team is responsible for updating our business continuity plans as new threats are identified. Customers are advised to regularly review their own security postures in conjunction with our updates."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you evaluate the potential impact of various disaster scenarios on your operations, and what metrics do you use?\nA: Kestrel Cloud evaluates disaster scenarios through our compliance program, focusing on ISO 22301 standards. We assess risks quarterly, utilizing metrics like downtime and service-level agreements (SLAs) to measure impact. Our control references guide the evaluation process, ensuring systematic identification of vulnerabilities. The responsibility for implementing disaster recovery plans is shared with clients, who must maintain their own backups and access controls."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you incorporate pandemic response planning into your overall business continuity strategy, and what key elements are included?\nA: Kestrel Cloud incorporates pandemic response planning into our business continuity strategy by adhering to our Compliance Assurance Framework. We conduct biannual reviews of our operational resilience plans, which include specific controls for pandemic scenarios. Our clients are responsible for their own data management during such events, while we ensure that Kestrel Cloud's infrastructure remains operational and secure. Our documented response procedures reference ISO 22301 standards, ensuring we remain compliant with industry best practices."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does senior management play in the approval and oversight of your disaster recovery and business continuity plans?\nA: Senior management at Kestrel Cloud Infrastructure is responsible for the approval of our disaster recovery and business continuity plans, which are aligned with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. These plans are reviewed annually to ensure they meet regulatory standards and operational requirements. Management's oversight includes regular audits and assessments, ensuring effective controls are in place to mitigate risks. Our clients are responsible for their own data backup and recovery processes within the Kestrel Cloud environment."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that all relevant stakeholders are informed about newly discovered vulnerabilities and the associated remediation efforts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict protocol to communicate vulnerabilities. We utilize our compliance program, VUL-Track, to notify stakeholders within 48 hours of discovery. This includes detailed remediation steps aligned with ISO 27001 standards. Customers are responsible for their own environments, but we ensure they receive timely updates to maintain compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What documentation is maintained during the triage process, and how is this information utilized to improve future incident response efforts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains incident reports and corrective action plans throughout the triage process. This documentation is integral to our compliance program, specifically aligning with ISO 27001 standards. We conduct quarterly reviews of these records to identify trends and implement necessary controls, ensuring our managed-container platform remains robust. Customer responsibilities are clearly outlined in our service agreements, emphasizing the shared nature of incident management."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place for conducting post-incident reviews, and how frequently are these reviews performed to assess the effectiveness of the incident response?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts post-incident reviews quarterly, as outlined in our Compliance Assurance Framework. Each review focuses on assessing the incident response process against our established controls, ensuring adherence to industry standards such as ISO 27001. Responsibilities for incident response are clearly defined, with our security team leading the review and reporting outcomes to management. This structured approach allows us to maintain compliance and enhance our incident management capabilities effectively."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you elaborate on the incident response procedures triggered by alerts generated from your logging and monitoring systems?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance frameworks, such as ISO 27001, to manage incident response. Alerts from our monitoring systems trigger an internal review within 30 minutes. Depending on the alert severity, our compliance team engages relevant stakeholders to determine necessary actions. Customers are responsible for incident reporting within their environments, while we ensure our infrastructure is monitored and secured continuously."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In the event of a security incident, what are the defined timelines for notifying affected customers, and how does your organization ensure compliance with these timelines?\nA: Kestrel Cloud notifies affected customers of security incidents within 48 hours, as outlined in our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Our incident response team follows strict protocols to ensure timely communication, and we leverage automated alert systems to facilitate this process. Adherence to these timelines is governed by internal controls and regular compliance checks against our established standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure that all stakeholders are informed of changes prior to implementation, and what communication methods are used?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous compliance program to ensure stakeholders are informed of changes before implementation. Notifications are sent out via our compliance management system at least 30 days prior to any significant updates. This ensures that all users are aware of changes and can adjust their operations accordingly. Our adherence to ISO 27001 standards reinforces our commitment to maintaining clear communication and control over the change management process."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In the event of a lost corporate device, what immediate response actions are taken to secure data and mitigate potential risks, and who is responsible for executing these actions?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict protocol for lost corporate devices. Upon notification, our compliance team activates a remote wipe within 15 minutes, as outlined in our Kestrel Compliance Program. The responsibility for reporting the incident rests with the employee, while our IT department ensures that all sensitive data is secured promptly. We adhere to industry standards, including ISO 27001, to guide our response actions."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does automation play in your vulnerability management process, particularly in the scanning and remediation phases?\nA: Kestrel Cloud utilizes automated tools for vulnerability scanning on a weekly basis, aligning with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Remediation actions are initiated based on scan results, with critical vulnerabilities addressed within 48 hours. The responsibility for securing customer workloads remains with the customer, as outlined in our shared-responsibility model. Automation enhances our ability to maintain compliance and security standards efficiently."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often are your DDoS protection measures reviewed and updated to address emerging threats and vulnerabilities?\nA: Kestrel Cloud reviews its DDoS protection measures quarterly as part of our compliance program. We adhere to the ISO 27001 standard and leverage our internal security assessments to ensure that our infrastructure remains resilient against evolving threats. Clients are responsible for their application-level security, while we maintain the integrity of our platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What steps do you take to engage third-party vendors in your business continuity planning, and how are their roles defined?\nA: Kestrel Cloud incorporates third-party vendors into our business continuity planning through our compliance program, which is aligned with industry standards like ISO 22301. We define vendor roles based on their specific service contributions and require them to submit annual continuity plans for review. This ensures that all parties understand their responsibilities, particularly in incident response. Our approach relies heavily on documented controls and regular assessments to maintain operational integrity."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization prioritize incidents during the triage process, and what criteria are used to determine the severity levels assigned to each incident?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict compliance program to categorize incidents. Severity levels are determined based on potential risk to infrastructure and customer data. Our triage process follows predefined control references, ensuring that critical incidents are escalated immediately while lower-severity cases are managed according to our internal guidelines. This allows for efficient resource allocation and timely resolution."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently is the personnel security training program updated to reflect current security threats and compliance requirements?\nA: Kestrel Cloud updates its personnel security training program quarterly, in line with our compliance framework, which includes ISO 27001 and NIST standards. This ensures that our team remains aware of evolving security threats and compliance obligations. We maintain a rigorous internal review process to guarantee that all training materials are current and relevant, while clients are responsible for their own security training and awareness."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What feedback mechanisms are in place to gather input from employees regarding the onboarding process and its impact on security awareness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a bi-annual review of the onboarding process, utilizing our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Feedback is collected through structured interviews with new hires, focusing on security awareness. This aligns with our ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that we maintain a high level of security consciousness among employees. Customer responsibility for security training is clearly defined in our service agreements."}
