{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What methods does your organization utilize for handling and storing evidence collected during audits to ensure its integrity and confidentiality?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict compliance protocols for handling audit evidence. Evidence is stored in a secure, encrypted environment, with access strictly controlled under our ISO 27001 compliance program. We retain audit records for a minimum of three years, ensuring they are only accessible to designated compliance officers. Regular reviews are conducted to verify adherence to our internal control standards, ensuring the integrity and confidentiality of all collected evidence."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes does your organization have in place to ensure that internal audits are conducted regularly and effectively to assess compliance with applicable standards and regulations?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts quarterly internal audits as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Assurance. These audits assess adherence to PCI-DSS and ISO 27017 standards. We leverage automated compliance tools to streamline the process, ensuring that all controls are tested regularly. The responsibility for compliance is shared with our customers, who must maintain their own security measures in line with our guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In what manner does your organization track and prioritize audit findings to ensure timely resolution and follow-up on identified issues?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to a rigorous compliance program, tracking audit findings via our internal compliance dashboard. Findings are prioritized based on risk assessments aligned with industry standards. We conduct monthly reviews to ensure timely resolutions, with designated compliance officers overseeing the process. The shared responsibility model delineates customer and vendor roles clearly, ensuring all parties are accountable for their respective areas."}
