{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What criteria does your organization use to determine whether an incident requires escalation to senior management or external parties, and how is this communicated?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict criteria outlined in our Compliance Framework. Incidents are escalated to senior management if they meet thresholds defined in our Incident Response Policy. Communication is executed via our internal ticketing system, ensuring prompt documentation and tracking. External parties are notified as per regulatory requirements. The customer is responsible for monitoring their environments to identify potential issues, while we manage the infrastructure layer."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you elaborate on the incident response procedures triggered by alerts generated from your logging and monitoring systems?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance frameworks, such as ISO 27001, to manage incident response. Alerts from our monitoring systems trigger an internal review within 30 minutes. Depending on the alert severity, our compliance team engages relevant stakeholders to determine necessary actions. Customers are responsible for incident reporting within their environments, while we ensure our infrastructure is monitored and secured continuously."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization track and document lessons learned from post-incident reviews, and what actions are taken to implement improvements based on these findings?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict compliance program that includes post-incident reviews. Each incident is logged in our Incident Management System, where we reference our internal control standards. Lessons learned are documented and reviewed quarterly, with improvement actions assigned to relevant teams. This process ensures that Kestrel Cloud maintains a high level of operational integrity and compliance with industry standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you document and review incidents of security policy violations to ensure that disciplinary actions are consistent and fair?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a strict protocol for documenting security policy violations, referencing our Compliance Framework. Incidents are logged immediately, and reviews occur bi-monthly. Disciplinary actions are aligned with our internal standards, ensuring uniformity. We leverage our incident response tools to facilitate this process, ensuring that all actions are traceable and compliant with our established guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place for conducting post-incident reviews, and how frequently are these reviews performed to assess the effectiveness of the incident response?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts post-incident reviews quarterly, as outlined in our Compliance Assurance Framework. Each review focuses on assessing the incident response process against our established controls, ensuring adherence to industry standards such as ISO 27001. Responsibilities for incident response are clearly defined, with our security team leading the review and reporting outcomes to management. This structured approach allows us to maintain compliance and enhance our incident management capabilities effectively."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the incident response procedures for handling detected anomalies in egress traffic?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous incident response framework that aligns with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Upon detection of anomalies in egress traffic, our team initiates a response within 30 minutes, leveraging automated alerting systems. The responsibility for monitoring and initial anomaly detection lies with the customer, while Kestrel Cloud manages the remediation processes and compliance reporting. Our adherence to industry standards ensures that all incidents are documented and reviewed systematically."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure that all employees are aware of policy exceptions that have been granted, and what training is provided?\nA: Kestrel Cloud ensures awareness of policy exceptions through our compliance program, which mandates biannual reviews and updates. Employees are required to complete training on policy exceptions as part of their onboarding process and annually thereafter. Our internal documentation references specific controls under ISO 27001, ensuring that all staff are aware of their responsibilities regarding exceptions. This structured approach minimizes risks and maintains compliance."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the process for reviewing and addressing findings from external audits, including how corrective actions are tracked and reported?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict protocol for reviewing external audit findings, adhering to our compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Assurance. Findings are evaluated within two weeks, and corrective actions are assigned to responsible teams. We utilize our Compliance Tracker tool to monitor progress and ensure timely resolution. Reports are generated quarterly to assess the effectiveness of our corrective measures and maintain compliance with industry standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What documentation is maintained during the triage process, and how is this information utilized to improve future incident response efforts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains incident reports and corrective action plans throughout the triage process. This documentation is integral to our compliance program, specifically aligning with ISO 27001 standards. We conduct quarterly reviews of these records to identify trends and implement necessary controls, ensuring our managed-container platform remains robust. Customer responsibilities are clearly outlined in our service agreements, emphasizing the shared nature of incident management."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you assess the effectiveness of your communication strategies during a disaster recovery event, and what feedback mechanisms are in place?\nA: Kestrel Cloud evaluates communication effectiveness during disaster recovery through our compliance program, specifically the Disaster Recovery Communication Standards. We implement a structured feedback loop post-event, ensuring that all stakeholders can provide input. Our internal audit team reviews these communications against established benchmarks every quarter, allowing us to refine our strategies continuously. Customers are responsible for notifying us of any communication gaps encountered during incidents."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you assess the effectiveness of your staff's understanding of encryption and key management protocols?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous compliance program to evaluate our staff's grasp of encryption and key management protocols. We conduct quarterly assessments aligned with ISO 27001 standards, ensuring our team is well-versed in current practices. Our internal audits focus on key management processes and encryption methodologies, reinforcing the importance of these protocols in our IaaS offerings. Staff training is mandatory, with completion rates tracked for compliance."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure compliance with applicable regulatory requirements during the incident response process, and what audits are conducted to verify this compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to its compliance program, which includes regular audits aligned with SOC 2 and PCI DSS standards. Our incident response process is reviewed quarterly to ensure regulatory compliance, with documented findings and corrective actions. Customers are responsible for their own data security, while we manage the infrastructure layer. This clear delineation of responsibilities is critical to maintaining compliance across our managed-container platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In what manner does your organization track and prioritize audit findings to ensure timely resolution and follow-up on identified issues?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to a rigorous compliance program, tracking audit findings via our internal compliance dashboard. Findings are prioritized based on risk assessments aligned with industry standards. We conduct monthly reviews to ensure timely resolutions, with designated compliance officers overseeing the process. The shared responsibility model delineates customer and vendor roles clearly, ensuring all parties are accountable for their respective areas."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In the event of a security incident, what are the defined timelines for notifying affected customers, and how does your organization ensure compliance with these timelines?\nA: Kestrel Cloud notifies affected customers of security incidents within 48 hours, as outlined in our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Our incident response team follows strict protocols to ensure timely communication, and we leverage automated alert systems to facilitate this process. Adherence to these timelines is governed by internal controls and regular compliance checks against our established standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that any exceptions to vulnerability management are periodically reviewed and reassessed for relevance and risk?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance standards, and we ensure that exceptions to vulnerability management are reviewed semi-annually. Our compliance program mandates that each exception is documented and assessed for risk, aligning with our internal control framework. This structured approach allows us to maintain a secure environment while ensuring that any exceptions remain relevant and justified."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently is the personnel security training program updated to reflect current security threats and compliance requirements?\nA: Kestrel Cloud updates its personnel security training program quarterly, in line with our compliance framework, which includes ISO 27001 and NIST standards. This ensures that our team remains aware of evolving security threats and compliance obligations. We maintain a rigorous internal review process to guarantee that all training materials are current and relevant, while clients are responsible for their own security training and awareness."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization communicate policy changes to all relevant stakeholders, and what methods are used to ensure understanding and compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud communicates policy changes via our compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework. Notifications are sent out bi-annually, and stakeholders are required to acknowledge receipt and understanding. Compliance with these updates is monitored through our internal audit processes, ensuring adherence to established control references. This structured approach minimizes ambiguity and reinforces the importance of compliance in our IaaS and managed-container services."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What criteria does your organization use to determine whether a change request requires formal approval, and who is responsible for granting that approval?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict compliance framework to determine change request approvals. Any modification impacting our infrastructure or services necessitates formal approval from the Change Control Committee, as outlined in our Compliance Program. We reference ISO 27001 standards for change management, ensuring consistency and security. Customers are responsible for notifying us of desired changes, but the final approval rests with our internal team to mitigate risks effectively."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes do you have in place for tracking the remediation of identified vulnerabilities, and how is progress reported to management?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a structured vulnerability remediation process defined by our compliance program, CloudSecure. Vulnerabilities are tracked through our internal ticketing system, with remediation timelines set in accordance with our Risk Management Framework. Progress is reported to management on a quarterly basis, ensuring alignment with our compliance objectives and industry standards such as ISO 27001. This enables us to maintain a high level of security across our IaaS platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe how your organization handles access requests and approvals for users who change roles within the company?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces strict role change protocols under our compliance program. Access requests are processed through our centralized management system, with approvals required from both the immediate supervisor and the security officer. The entire process is governed by our internal standard KCP-12, ensuring timely updates within 24 hours. All role changes are logged for audit purposes, and customers must ensure their internal policies align with these requirements."}
