{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What feedback mechanisms are in place to gather input from employees regarding the onboarding process and its impact on security awareness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a bi-annual review of the onboarding process, utilizing our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Feedback is collected through structured interviews with new hires, focusing on security awareness. This aligns with our ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that we maintain a high level of security consciousness among employees. Customer responsibility for security training is clearly defined in our service agreements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently is the personnel security training program updated to reflect current security threats and compliance requirements?\nA: Kestrel Cloud updates its personnel security training program quarterly, in line with our compliance framework, which includes ISO 27001 and NIST standards. This ensures that our team remains aware of evolving security threats and compliance obligations. We maintain a rigorous internal review process to guarantee that all training materials are current and relevant, while clients are responsible for their own security training and awareness."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the procedures followed during the onboarding process to ensure that new employees understand security policies and their responsibilities?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a stringent onboarding procedure that aligns with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. New hires receive immediate access to our security policy documentation and complete mandatory training within their first week. This training references ISO 27001 standards and emphasizes the importance of data integrity and confidentiality. Employees are required to acknowledge their understanding of these policies as part of the onboarding process."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often does your organization conduct training and awareness programs related to security governance for all employees, and what topics are covered?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts mandatory security governance training annually for all personnel. Our program aligns with ISO 27001 and NIST standards, covering compliance, risk management, and incident response. Employees are required to complete this training to ensure adherence to our stringent compliance framework. This program is critical in maintaining our secure IaaS and managed-container services."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What training programs are in place to ensure that your staff understands the importance of network security and segmentation?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a rigorous training program as part of our compliance framework. Staff members complete annual training on network security and segmentation, referencing our internal compliance standards, including KCI-SEC-001 and KCI-SEC-002. This training is mandatory for all employees and is designed to ensure that everyone understands their role in maintaining the security of the Kestrel Cloud platform. Regular assessments are conducted to evaluate knowledge retention and application in day-to-day operations."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you maintain awareness of emerging threats that could impact your business continuity, and what process do you follow to adapt your plans accordingly?\nA: Kestrel Cloud leverages its compliance program to stay informed about emerging threats. We conduct biannual reviews of our infrastructure against industry standards, including ISO 27001 and NIST. Our incident response team is responsible for updating our business continuity plans as new threats are identified. Customers are advised to regularly review their own security postures in conjunction with our updates."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure that all stakeholders are aware of their roles and responsibilities regarding the governance of the security program?\nA: Kestrel Cloud ensures stakeholder awareness of security governance roles through our compliance program, which mandates biannual reviews of responsibilities. We reference ISO 27001 and NIST standards, aligning our internal controls with industry best practices. Each stakeholder is assigned a specific role within our governance framework, ensuring clarity and accountability in security management."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In what ways are employees informed about the consequences of non-compliance with security policies and the disciplinary process?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces strict adherence to security policies through our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Employees receive biannual training on the disciplinary measures associated with non-compliance, which are clearly outlined in our security manual. Non-compliance can lead to immediate review and potential disciplinary action as per our established protocols."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What training do you provide to employees regarding data classification and privacy obligations?\nA: Kestrel Cloud provides annual training on data classification and privacy obligations as part of our compliance program. Employees are required to complete our Kestrel Compliance Training, which is aligned with ISO 27001 standards. This training emphasizes the importance of data handling and the roles employees play in maintaining security. We also conduct quarterly refreshers to ensure ongoing awareness and adherence to our policies."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does senior management play in promoting a culture of compliance and risk awareness within the organization, and how is this communicated to staff?\nA: Senior management at Kestrel Cloud emphasizes compliance through our Kestrel Compliance Program, which includes regular audits and risk assessments. Staff are informed via mandatory training sessions held bi-annually, ensuring that everyone understands their responsibilities regarding compliance and risk management. Our control references are updated regularly to reflect the latest standards, and adherence is monitored continuously to maintain a secure infrastructure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that all relevant stakeholders are informed about newly discovered vulnerabilities and the associated remediation efforts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict protocol to communicate vulnerabilities. We utilize our compliance program, VUL-Track, to notify stakeholders within 48 hours of discovery. This includes detailed remediation steps aligned with ISO 27001 standards. Customers are responsible for their own environments, but we ensure they receive timely updates to maintain compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What steps do you take to ensure that your encryption practices remain effective against evolving cybersecurity threats?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous compliance program, including regular reviews of our encryption protocols aligned with NIST standards. We conduct quarterly assessments to ensure our encryption methods, including TLS 1.3 for data in transit, remain effective. Customers are responsible for managing their own encryption keys, while we focus on maintaining a secure infrastructure. Our internal audits ensure that we adapt swiftly to any new threats identified in the cybersecurity landscape."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific tools or technologies does your organization employ to detect security incidents in real-time, and how are these integrated into your overall security architecture?\nA: Kestrel Cloud utilizes a robust suite of monitoring tools, including our proprietary compliance dashboard and third-party intrusion detection systems, to ensure real-time incident detection. Our compliance framework aligns with industry standards such as ISO 27001 and SOC 2, and we conduct regular assessments to maintain these certifications. Clients are responsible for their own application-level security, while we handle infrastructure monitoring and alerting through automated systems."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific procedures does your organization follow to contain security incidents once they are detected, and how are these procedures communicated to relevant stakeholders?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict incident management protocol aligned with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Upon detection of a security incident, containment measures are enacted within 30 minutes, followed by a detailed analysis. Relevant stakeholders are notified through our secure communication channels. Our incident response is guided by industry standards, ensuring we maintain control over our infrastructure while clearly delineating customer responsibilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific hardening configurations are applied to corporate devices before they are issued to employees, and how are these configurations documented?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements hardening configurations on corporate devices by adhering to our compliance program, specifically the Kestrel Secure Framework. This includes applying security patches bi-weekly and enforcing encryption standards. Documentation is maintained in our centralized compliance repository, ensuring all configurations are traceable and auditable. Responsibility for maintaining these configurations lies with our IT security team, while users are expected to follow established usage policies."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In what manner does your organization report security risks and compliance status to the board, and how often are these reports generated and reviewed?\nA: Kestrel Cloud generates compliance and risk reports for the board on a monthly basis. Our internal compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework, dictates the structure and content of these reports. We reference NIST standards and ensure that all findings are clearly communicated to the board. The focus is on identifying any deviations from compliance requirements and outlining the corrective actions needed, ensuring that the board is always informed of our security status."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization incorporate feedback from previous audits into the planning and execution of future audits to enhance overall effectiveness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud incorporates audit feedback into our compliance program through a structured review process. We conduct audits quarterly, referencing our internal control frameworks and industry standards. Feedback is analyzed for trends and incorporated into our risk management strategies. This ensures that Kestrel Cloud remains aligned with best practices and regulatory requirements, enhancing our managed-container platform's security posture."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you explain the process for reviewing and approving changes to firewall configurations, including who is involved?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict change management process for firewall configurations. Changes are reviewed bi-weekly by our security team and must align with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Approval requires sign-off from both the security officer and the infrastructure manager. This ensures that all changes are documented and controlled according to our internal standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place for the identification, assessment, and documentation of risks within your risk register, and how frequently is this register updated?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a risk register that is reviewed bi-annually, adhering to our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Risks are assessed against internal controls and documented systematically. Each risk is assigned to designated control owners, ensuring accountability. We reference NIST SP 800-53 for control frameworks, emphasizing our commitment to compliance and security. Customers are responsible for their application-level risks."}
