{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What methods do you use to monitor and control outbound traffic to ensure compliance with security policies and prevent data leakage?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs strict outbound traffic controls as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. We utilize automated monitoring tools that assess traffic against predefined security policies. All outbound traffic is logged and reviewed weekly to ensure adherence to compliance standards. The responsibility for data classification and policy enforcement lies primarily with the customer, while we facilitate the necessary controls to support their efforts."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you detail the authentication methods used for remote access, including any multi-factor authentication processes in place?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a stringent authentication framework for remote access, mandating multi-factor authentication in line with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure Access. Users must authenticate via a secure password followed by a second factor, typically a hardware token or mobile app verification. This ensures that access is tightly controlled and monitored, aligning with industry best practices and regulatory requirements. The responsibility for managing user access roles lies with our clients, ensuring they maintain appropriate governance over their environments."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What protocols and technologies are employed for secure remote access to your network, and how do you ensure they are regularly updated?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs TLS for secure remote access and adheres to our Compliance Framework, which includes regular audits. We ensure that all access protocols are reviewed and updated annually, in line with our internal security policies. Clients are responsible for managing their own access controls, while we maintain the infrastructure and compliance standards necessary for secure operations."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What logging practices are in place for egress traffic, and how long is this data retained for forensic analysis?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains strict logging practices for egress traffic as part of our compliance program. We log relevant egress traffic data for a duration of 30 days, following the standards set forth in our Kestrel Compliance Framework. This data includes essential metadata necessary for audit trails. Customers are responsible for their own logging configurations, and we provide APIs to facilitate this process as needed."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What mechanisms are in place to monitor and log traffic at the perimeter of your network to detect unauthorized access attempts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud integrates perimeter security measures with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. We utilize automated logging mechanisms that capture all incoming and outgoing traffic for analysis. Our monitoring tools, aligned with ISO 27001 standards, provide real-time alerts for unauthorized access attempts. Customers are required to maintain their own security configurations while we oversee the infrastructure's integrity. Logs are reviewed bi-weekly to ensure compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What mechanisms are in place to monitor and log access to sensitive data and systems, and how often are these logs reviewed?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs continuous monitoring mechanisms for access to sensitive data. Logs are generated for all access events and are retained for a minimum of 90 days. Our compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework, mandates quarterly reviews of these logs to ensure adherence to standards such as ISO 27001. Customers are responsible for configuring their access controls within the platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that egress controls are effectively implemented to prevent unauthorized data exfiltration from your network?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces egress controls through our compliance program, which adheres to ISO 27001 standards. We utilize automated tools to monitor and log all outbound traffic, ensuring that any unauthorized attempts are flagged immediately. Our customers are responsible for configuring their own security groups, but we provide guidelines to streamline this process. Regular internal audits verify the effectiveness of our controls, maintaining a secure environment for all users of Kestrel Cloud."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you manage and log access to sensitive areas within your data centers, and what audits are conducted to review this access?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs strict access controls to sensitive areas, with logging managed through our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Access logs are reviewed bi-annually, ensuring adherence to industry standards. We leverage automated tools for real-time monitoring and audits, which are integral to our compliance framework. Customers are responsible for managing their own access within the cloud environment, while we maintain oversight of physical data center entry."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure the integrity of logs once they are generated, and what specific mechanisms are in place to prevent unauthorized alterations?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a comprehensive logging strategy that includes immutable log storage and strict access controls per our compliance program. We utilize tools like AWS CloudTrail and Azure Monitor to ensure logs are generated in a manner that prevents unauthorized alterations. Logs are retained for a minimum of 90 days, and any access is logged and monitored to ensure compliance with our internal policies. Customers must manage their own log access but can rely on our infrastructure to maintain log integrity."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization handle exceptions to standard access control policies, and what approval process is followed?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict compliance program for handling access control exceptions. Any deviation from standard policies requires documented approval from a designated Compliance Officer. This process is in line with our ISO 27001 framework. Requests are logged and tracked for audit purposes, ensuring accountability and traceability. We emphasize the importance of adhering to these controls to maintain the security posture of Kestrel Cloud."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure that access rights are promptly revoked when an employee leaves the company?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict compliance program that mandates immediate revocation of access rights when an employee exits. Within 12 hours of termination, all access to Kestrel Cloud services is disabled through our automated identity management system. This process aligns with our internal security standards and ensures that all user roles are promptly updated to prevent unauthorized access."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place to review and update access control policies, and how often are these reviews conducted?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to a strict compliance program, reviewing access control policies quarterly. Our policy review process is aligned with ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that controls are effective and up to date. Access controls are managed through our centralized compliance platform, which tracks changes and audits access logs. Customers are responsible for managing their own user access within the parameters we provide, ensuring a clear delineation of responsibilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What methods does your organization employ to authenticate users before granting access to sensitive systems and data?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict authentication process that includes multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access controls (RBAC). Our compliance program, Kestrel Secure, mandates regular reviews of access logs and user permissions to ensure adherence to ISO 27001 standards. Customers are responsible for managing their own user credentials and access policies, while we provide the necessary tools and guidelines for secure implementation."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the processes in place for managing privileged access, including how privileges are granted and revoked?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs strict access controls as part of our compliance program. Privileged access is granted through a centralized identity management system, with roles defined by our internal standards. Revocation of privileges occurs immediately upon termination or role change. Regular audits are conducted to ensure adherence to these controls, and any deviations are addressed promptly."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often does your organization reassess the effectiveness of its authentication methods, particularly in response to emerging threats?\nA: Kestrel Cloud reassesses authentication methods biannually, guided by our compliance program, Kestrel Secure Framework. This framework aligns with industry standards such as ISO 27001 and NIST. We leverage automated monitoring tools to ensure ongoing effectiveness, while customers are responsible for managing their own user access policies. This clear delineation of responsibilities supports our clients in maintaining a secure environment within Kestrel Cloud."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role do automated tools play in managing and enforcing egress controls across your network?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs automated tools to enforce egress controls as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Guard. These tools continuously monitor data egress points and ensure adherence to our established security standards. We maintain strict control over egress traffic, and while our tools provide significant oversight, customers must actively participate in defining their specific egress policies to align with their compliance requirements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you manage and document key access requests, and who has the authority to approve such requests?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict access control framework governed by our Compliance Program. Key access requests are logged and reviewed monthly, with approvals granted solely by designated compliance officers. This process adheres to ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that only authorized personnel can access sensitive information. Customers are responsible for managing their own user permissions within the Kestrel Cloud platform, maintaining a clear delineation of responsibilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently is the physical access control system reviewed and updated to ensure its effectiveness against unauthorized access?\nA: Kestrel Cloud performs a review of physical access controls quarterly, aligning with our compliance program standards. We reference the ISO 27001 framework to guide our assessments and ensure all controls remain effective against unauthorized access. The responsibility for maintaining physical security is shared with our customers, who are encouraged to implement their own access measures alongside our infrastructure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization evaluate the effectiveness of its identity and access management practices in mitigating risks?\nA: Kestrel Cloud evaluates its identity and access management practices through a rigorous compliance framework aligned with our Kestrel Compliance Program. We conduct biannual assessments against industry standards such as ISO 27001 and NIST 800-53. Access controls are reviewed quarterly, ensuring that all roles are appropriately assigned and monitored. Customers are responsible for managing their own access policies, while we provide the necessary tools and logs for oversight."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific measures are in place to control physical access to your data centers, including the use of identification badges or biometric systems?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs stringent physical access controls at our data centers, adhering to our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Access is limited to authorized personnel only, using identification badges and biometric verification. All entry points are monitored 24/7 with CCTV, and access logs are maintained for auditing purposes. Customers are responsible for ensuring that their access credentials are managed securely, as part of our shared responsibility model."}
