{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What documentation is maintained regarding your cryptographic policies and procedures, and how is this documentation kept up to date?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a robust set of documentation for our cryptographic policies, adhering to the ISO 27001 standard. This documentation is reviewed annually as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Secure, to ensure it meets evolving regulatory requirements. We emphasize that customers are responsible for managing their own encryption keys, while we provide the necessary tools and infrastructure for secure data handling. Our policies are accessible through our compliance portal for transparency."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place to manage sensitive information such as API keys and secrets throughout the application lifecycle?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous compliance program that mandates the use of encryption for all API keys and secrets. Access is strictly controlled through role-based access management, and we conduct quarterly reviews to ensure adherence to our internal standards. Customers are responsible for managing their own secrets within their environments, while we provide the necessary tools and documentation to facilitate secure practices."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe any third-party audits or assessments that have been conducted on your cryptographic practices, and what were the outcomes?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts biannual assessments of our cryptographic controls as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. These evaluations are aligned with ISO 27001 and SOC 2 Type II standards. Recent audits verified our strong encryption protocols, but highlighted areas for improvement in customer-managed encryption keys. Our clients are responsible for key management, ensuring they understand their role in our shared responsibility model."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe your approach to managing and securing third-party dependencies within your applications, including any automated tools used?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance frameworks, including ISO 27001 and SOC 2, to manage third-party dependencies. Our automated tools, such as Black Duck and Checkmarx, conduct regular scans of all integrated libraries. We perform these scans quarterly, ensuring that any vulnerabilities are addressed promptly. Clients are reminded that they share responsibility for the security of their applications, particularly in how they configure and utilize our managed-container services."}
