{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes does your organization have in place to ensure that internal audits are conducted regularly and effectively to assess compliance with applicable standards and regulations?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts quarterly internal audits as part of our compliance program, Kestrel Assurance. These audits assess adherence to PCI-DSS and ISO 27017 standards. We leverage automated compliance tools to streamline the process, ensuring that all controls are tested regularly. The responsibility for compliance is shared with our customers, who must maintain their own security measures in line with our guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization ensure compliance with applicable regulatory requirements during the incident response process, and what audits are conducted to verify this compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to its compliance program, which includes regular audits aligned with SOC 2 and PCI DSS standards. Our incident response process is reviewed quarterly to ensure regulatory compliance, with documented findings and corrective actions. Customers are responsible for their own data security, while we manage the infrastructure layer. This clear delineation of responsibilities is critical to maintaining compliance across our managed-container platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often do you conduct audits to evaluate adherence to your data classification and retention policies?\nA: Kestrel Cloud performs audits quarterly to ensure compliance with our data classification and retention policies. Our internal compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework, guides these evaluations. We leverage automated compliance checks and manual reviews to uphold our standards. Customers are responsible for their own data classification, while we ensure the infrastructure meets necessary regulations."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization incorporate feedback from previous audits into the planning and execution of future audits to enhance overall effectiveness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud incorporates audit feedback into our compliance program through a structured review process. We conduct audits quarterly, referencing our internal control frameworks and industry standards. Feedback is analyzed for trends and incorporated into our risk management strategies. This ensures that Kestrel Cloud remains aligned with best practices and regulatory requirements, enhancing our managed-container platform's security posture."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you maintain records of data classification decisions and the rationale behind them?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance standards, maintaining records of data classification decisions in our compliance management system. These records are reviewed biannually, ensuring alignment with our internal policies and regulatory requirements. The responsibility for classification rests with the customer, while we provide the necessary tools and frameworks to support their efforts. Our compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework, guides these processes."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that your logging practices comply with relevant regulatory requirements, and what steps are taken to maintain this compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict compliance protocols as outlined in our Kestrel Compliance Framework. Our logging practices are aligned with NIST SP 800-53 standards, ensuring that all logs are generated, stored, and reviewed in accordance with regulatory requirements. We implement automated monitoring tools that facilitate real-time compliance checks. Customers are responsible for configuring their own logging settings, while we ensure the underlying infrastructure meets compliance mandates."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization communicate policy changes to all relevant stakeholders, and what methods are used to ensure understanding and compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud communicates policy changes via our compliance program, Kestrel Compliance Framework. Notifications are sent out bi-annually, and stakeholders are required to acknowledge receipt and understanding. Compliance with these updates is monitored through our internal audit processes, ensuring adherence to established control references. This structured approach minimizes ambiguity and reinforces the importance of compliance in our IaaS and managed-container services."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure compliance with industry standards and regulations related to vulnerability management, and what audits or assessments do you conduct to verify this compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a rigorous compliance program, aligning with standards such as SOC 2 and PCI DSS. We conduct bi-annual internal audits and utilize automated tools to continuously monitor vulnerabilities. Our compliance framework, known as Kestrel Compliance Assurance, ensures that all controls are regularly tested and updated. Customers are responsible for their container configurations, while we manage the underlying infrastructure security. This clear division of responsibilities allows us to maintain a secure environment for Kestrel Cloud users."}
