{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does senior management play in promoting a culture of compliance and risk awareness within the organization, and how is this communicated to staff?\nA: Senior management at Kestrel Cloud emphasizes compliance through our Kestrel Compliance Program, which includes regular audits and risk assessments. Staff are informed via mandatory training sessions held bi-annually, ensuring that everyone understands their responsibilities regarding compliance and risk management. Our control references are updated regularly to reflect the latest standards, and adherence is monitored continuously to maintain a secure infrastructure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure compliance with relevant regulations and standards in your business continuity and disaster recovery planning?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains compliance with our internal Kestrel Compliance Framework, which is aligned with NIST SP 800-34 and ISO 27031. Our business continuity and disaster recovery plans are reviewed quarterly to ensure they meet these standards. We rely on automated tools for backup and recovery processes, and customers are responsible for their own data redundancy strategies. Regular training sessions for our staff ensure everyone understands their roles in maintaining compliance."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you manage and log access to sensitive areas within your data centers, and what audits are conducted to review this access?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs strict access controls to sensitive areas, with logging managed through our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Access logs are reviewed bi-annually, ensuring adherence to industry standards. We leverage automated tools for real-time monitoring and audits, which are integral to our compliance framework. Customers are responsible for managing their own access within the cloud environment, while we maintain oversight of physical data center entry."}
