{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What criteria does your organization use to determine the need for multi-factor authentication for different user groups?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a risk-based approach to determine MFA requirements across user groups. Our compliance program, including ISO 27001 and SOC 2, guides us in identifying high-risk roles that necessitate MFA. Users in administrative or privileged roles are mandated to use MFA, while standard users may not be. This framework is critical to maintaining the integrity of our IaaS and managed-container services."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What methods does your organization employ to authenticate users before granting access to sensitive systems and data?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict authentication process that includes multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access controls (RBAC). Our compliance program, Kestrel Secure, mandates regular reviews of access logs and user permissions to ensure adherence to ISO 27001 standards. Customers are responsible for managing their own user credentials and access policies, while we provide the necessary tools and guidelines for secure implementation."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you explain the process for reviewing and approving changes to firewall configurations, including who is involved?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict change management process for firewall configurations. Changes are reviewed bi-weekly by our security team and must align with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Approval requires sign-off from both the security officer and the infrastructure manager. This ensures that all changes are documented and controlled according to our internal standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific procedures does your organization follow to contain security incidents once they are detected, and how are these procedures communicated to relevant stakeholders?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict incident management protocol aligned with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Upon detection of a security incident, containment measures are enacted within 30 minutes, followed by a detailed analysis. Relevant stakeholders are notified through our secure communication channels. Our incident response is guided by industry standards, ensuring we maintain control over our infrastructure while clearly delineating customer responsibilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What feedback mechanisms are in place to gather input from employees regarding the onboarding process and its impact on security awareness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a bi-annual review of the onboarding process, utilizing our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Feedback is collected through structured interviews with new hires, focusing on security awareness. This aligns with our ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that we maintain a high level of security consciousness among employees. Customer responsibility for security training is clearly defined in our service agreements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you document and review incidents of security policy violations to ensure that disciplinary actions are consistent and fair?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a strict protocol for documenting security policy violations, referencing our Compliance Framework. Incidents are logged immediately, and reviews occur bi-monthly. Disciplinary actions are aligned with our internal standards, ensuring uniformity. We leverage our incident response tools to facilitate this process, ensuring that all actions are traceable and compliant with our established guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place for conducting post-incident reviews, and how frequently are these reviews performed to assess the effectiveness of the incident response?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts post-incident reviews quarterly, as outlined in our Compliance Assurance Framework. Each review focuses on assessing the incident response process against our established controls, ensuring adherence to industry standards such as ISO 27001. Responsibilities for incident response are clearly defined, with our security team leading the review and reporting outcomes to management. This structured approach allows us to maintain compliance and enhance our incident management capabilities effectively."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What criteria does your organization use to determine whether an incident requires escalation to senior management or external parties, and how is this communicated?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict criteria outlined in our Compliance Framework. Incidents are escalated to senior management if they meet thresholds defined in our Incident Response Policy. Communication is executed via our internal ticketing system, ensuring prompt documentation and tracking. External parties are notified as per regulatory requirements. The customer is responsible for monitoring their environments to identify potential issues, while we manage the infrastructure layer."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the roles and responsibilities of personnel involved in the incident triage process, and how they are trained to handle various incident types?\nA: Kestrel Cloud's incident triage personnel are trained under our KCI Compliance Program, focusing on rapid response to infrastructure incidents. Responsibilities include initial assessment and escalation to specialized teams. Training is ongoing, with quarterly reviews of incident response protocols. Customers retain responsibility for their data security within the Kestrel Cloud environment, aligning with our shared responsibility model."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often does your organization conduct training and awareness programs related to security governance for all employees, and what topics are covered?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts mandatory security governance training annually for all personnel. Our program aligns with ISO 27001 and NIST standards, covering compliance, risk management, and incident response. Employees are required to complete this training to ensure adherence to our stringent compliance framework. This program is critical in maintaining our secure IaaS and managed-container services."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the incident response procedures for handling detected anomalies in egress traffic?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous incident response framework that aligns with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Upon detection of anomalies in egress traffic, our team initiates a response within 30 minutes, leveraging automated alerting systems. The responsibility for monitoring and initial anomaly detection lies with the customer, while Kestrel Cloud manages the remediation processes and compliance reporting. Our adherence to industry standards ensures that all incidents are documented and reviewed systematically."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What mechanisms are in place to monitor and log traffic at the perimeter of your network to detect unauthorized access attempts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud integrates perimeter security measures with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. We utilize automated logging mechanisms that capture all incoming and outgoing traffic for analysis. Our monitoring tools, aligned with ISO 27001 standards, provide real-time alerts for unauthorized access attempts. Customers are required to maintain their own security configurations while we oversee the infrastructure's integrity. Logs are reviewed bi-weekly to ensure compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In the event of a security incident, what are the defined timelines for notifying affected customers, and how does your organization ensure compliance with these timelines?\nA: Kestrel Cloud notifies affected customers of security incidents within 48 hours, as outlined in our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Our incident response team follows strict protocols to ensure timely communication, and we leverage automated alert systems to facilitate this process. Adherence to these timelines is governed by internal controls and regular compliance checks against our established standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you elaborate on the incident response procedures triggered by alerts generated from your logging and monitoring systems?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to strict compliance frameworks, such as ISO 27001, to manage incident response. Alerts from our monitoring systems trigger an internal review within 30 minutes. Depending on the alert severity, our compliance team engages relevant stakeholders to determine necessary actions. Customers are responsible for incident reporting within their environments, while we ensure our infrastructure is monitored and secured continuously."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization handle exceptions to standard access control policies, and what approval process is followed?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict compliance program for handling access control exceptions. Any deviation from standard policies requires documented approval from a designated Compliance Officer. This process is in line with our ISO 27001 framework. Requests are logged and tracked for audit purposes, ensuring accountability and traceability. We emphasize the importance of adhering to these controls to maintain the security posture of Kestrel Cloud."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What protocols do you have for handling visitors in your data centers, particularly regarding their identification and supervision during access?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces strict access control for data center visitors. All visitors are required to undergo identity verification and are monitored at all times during their stay. Our compliance program, Kestrel Secure Access (KSA), mandates that visitors are logged in our system and escorted by security personnel. This ensures adherence to our internal control standards and minimizes risk. We take visitor management seriously and continuously improve our protocols to align with industry best practices."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently is the personnel security training program updated to reflect current security threats and compliance requirements?\nA: Kestrel Cloud updates its personnel security training program quarterly, in line with our compliance framework, which includes ISO 27001 and NIST standards. This ensures that our team remains aware of evolving security threats and compliance obligations. We maintain a rigorous internal review process to guarantee that all training materials are current and relevant, while clients are responsible for their own security training and awareness."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific tools or technologies does your organization employ to detect security incidents in real-time, and how are these integrated into your overall security architecture?\nA: Kestrel Cloud utilizes a robust suite of monitoring tools, including our proprietary compliance dashboard and third-party intrusion detection systems, to ensure real-time incident detection. Our compliance framework aligns with industry standards such as ISO 27001 and SOC 2, and we conduct regular assessments to maintain these certifications. Clients are responsible for their own application-level security, while we handle infrastructure monitoring and alerting through automated systems."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you detail the authentication methods used for remote access, including any multi-factor authentication processes in place?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a stringent authentication framework for remote access, mandating multi-factor authentication in line with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure Access. Users must authenticate via a secure password followed by a second factor, typically a hardware token or mobile app verification. This ensures that access is tightly controlled and monitored, aligning with industry best practices and regulatory requirements. The responsibility for managing user access roles lies with our clients, ensuring they maintain appropriate governance over their environments."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe how your organization handles access requests and approvals for users who change roles within the company?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces strict role change protocols under our compliance program. Access requests are processed through our centralized management system, with approvals required from both the immediate supervisor and the security officer. The entire process is governed by our internal standard KCP-12, ensuring timely updates within 24 hours. All role changes are logged for audit purposes, and customers must ensure their internal policies align with these requirements."}
