{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes do you have in place for tracking the remediation of identified vulnerabilities, and how is progress reported to management?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a structured vulnerability remediation process defined by our compliance program, CloudSecure. Vulnerabilities are tracked through our internal ticketing system, with remediation timelines set in accordance with our Risk Management Framework. Progress is reported to management on a quarterly basis, ensuring alignment with our compliance objectives and industry standards such as ISO 27001. This enables us to maintain a high level of security across our IaaS platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What metrics do you use to measure the effectiveness of your vulnerability management program, and how are these metrics reported to stakeholders?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous set of metrics to gauge our vulnerability management program's effectiveness, including compliance with ISO 27001 and the frequency of vulnerability scans. Reports are generated bi-monthly and shared with stakeholders as part of our compliance program. Our control references guide the remediation process, ensuring that vulnerabilities are addressed promptly. Customers retain responsibility for their configurations and deployed applications, which is critical for maintaining overall security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Who is responsible for overseeing the vulnerability management program, and what qualifications or expertise do they possess in this area?\nA: Kestrel Cloud's vulnerability management program is overseen by our Compliance Officer, who is certified in ISO 27001 and SOC 2 frameworks. We conduct quarterly vulnerability scans and adhere to our internal compliance program, which includes regular audits against NIST standards. Customers are responsible for securing their own applications and data within the Kestrel Cloud environment, while we ensure the infrastructure is fortified against known vulnerabilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What is your policy regarding the documentation and remediation of identified security vulnerabilities within your applications, including timelines for resolution?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict compliance program that mandates the documentation and remediation of security vulnerabilities. We classify vulnerabilities by severity and target resolution timelines of 14 days for critical issues and 30 days for high-severity ones. Our internal control framework ensures that these timelines are adhered to, with regular audits to verify compliance. Customers are responsible for their own configurations, and we provide guidelines to help them mitigate risks effectively."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does automation play in your vulnerability management process, particularly in the scanning and remediation phases?\nA: Kestrel Cloud utilizes automated tools for vulnerability scanning on a weekly basis, aligning with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Remediation actions are initiated based on scan results, with critical vulnerabilities addressed within 48 hours. The responsibility for securing customer workloads remains with the customer, as outlined in our shared-responsibility model. Automation enhances our ability to maintain compliance and security standards efficiently."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that all relevant stakeholders are informed about newly discovered vulnerabilities and the associated remediation efforts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict protocol to communicate vulnerabilities. We utilize our compliance program, VUL-Track, to notify stakeholders within 48 hours of discovery. This includes detailed remediation steps aligned with ISO 27001 standards. Customers are responsible for their own environments, but we ensure they receive timely updates to maintain compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What tools or technologies do you utilize for vulnerability scanning, and how do you evaluate their effectiveness in identifying threats?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs Rapid7 and OpenVAS for vulnerability scanning. Our compliance program mandates quarterly assessments to ensure robust threat identification. We reference ISO 27001 and NIST standards to evaluate the effectiveness of these tools, aligning our findings with our internal risk management framework. Customers are responsible for their own configurations, while we ensure the underlying infrastructure is secure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the criteria used to classify vulnerabilities by severity, and how often are these criteria reviewed and updated?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a severity classification system based on NIST SP 800-53 controls. Vulnerabilities are assessed for impact and likelihood, with critical issues addressed immediately. Our compliance program mandates a quarterly review of these criteria to ensure they remain relevant. Customers are responsible for their own application-level security, while we manage the underlying infrastructure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific procedures does your organization follow to contain security incidents once they are detected, and how are these procedures communicated to relevant stakeholders?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict incident management protocol aligned with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Upon detection of a security incident, containment measures are enacted within 30 minutes, followed by a detailed analysis. Relevant stakeholders are notified through our secure communication channels. Our incident response is guided by industry standards, ensuring we maintain control over our infrastructure while clearly delineating customer responsibilities."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What processes are in place to update your encryption practices in response to emerging threats or vulnerabilities?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict compliance program that mandates quarterly reviews of our encryption practices. We reference industry standards such as NIST and ISO 27001 to guide our updates. Any identified vulnerabilities trigger an immediate assessment, followed by necessary changes. Our customers are responsible for their encryption keys, while we ensure our infrastructure remains secure and compliant."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific measures do you have in place to secure your APIs against common vulnerabilities, such as injection attacks or improper authentication?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a rigorous compliance program that adheres to industry standards such as ISO 27001 and NIST. We conduct quarterly security audits and utilize automated tools to detect and prevent injection attacks. Our API gateway enforces strong authentication mechanisms, ensuring that only authorized users can access resources. Customers are responsible for API key management, while we maintain the infrastructure security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you document and review incidents of security policy violations to ensure that disciplinary actions are consistent and fair?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a strict protocol for documenting security policy violations, referencing our Compliance Framework. Incidents are logged immediately, and reviews occur bi-monthly. Disciplinary actions are aligned with our internal standards, ensuring uniformity. We leverage our incident response tools to facilitate this process, ensuring that all actions are traceable and compliant with our established guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific secure design principles are integrated into your application development lifecycle to mitigate security vulnerabilities during the initial design phase?\nA: Kestrel Cloud incorporates secure design principles by adhering to our compliance program, which includes regular security assessments and risk management protocols. Our development lifecycle is governed by ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that security is embedded from the outset. We maintain strict control over access management and code reviews, with a focus on minimizing vulnerabilities. Customers are responsible for their configurations, while we ensure the underlying infrastructure remains secure."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What specific tools or technologies does your organization employ to detect security incidents in real-time, and how are these integrated into your overall security architecture?\nA: Kestrel Cloud utilizes a robust suite of monitoring tools, including our proprietary compliance dashboard and third-party intrusion detection systems, to ensure real-time incident detection. Our compliance framework aligns with industry standards such as ISO 27001 and SOC 2, and we conduct regular assessments to maintain these certifications. Clients are responsible for their own application-level security, while we handle infrastructure monitoring and alerting through automated systems."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you explain the process for reviewing and approving changes to firewall configurations, including who is involved?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a strict change management process for firewall configurations. Changes are reviewed bi-weekly by our security team and must align with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Approval requires sign-off from both the security officer and the infrastructure manager. This ensures that all changes are documented and controlled according to our internal standards."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What mechanisms are in place to monitor and log traffic at the perimeter of your network to detect unauthorized access attempts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud integrates perimeter security measures with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. We utilize automated logging mechanisms that capture all incoming and outgoing traffic for analysis. Our monitoring tools, aligned with ISO 27001 standards, provide real-time alerts for unauthorized access attempts. Customers are required to maintain their own security configurations while we oversee the infrastructure's integrity. Logs are reviewed bi-weekly to ensure compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often are your DDoS protection measures reviewed and updated to address emerging threats and vulnerabilities?\nA: Kestrel Cloud reviews its DDoS protection measures quarterly as part of our compliance program. We adhere to the ISO 27001 standard and leverage our internal security assessments to ensure that our infrastructure remains resilient against evolving threats. Clients are responsible for their application-level security, while we maintain the integrity of our platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What feedback mechanisms are in place to gather input from employees regarding the onboarding process and its impact on security awareness?\nA: Kestrel Cloud implements a bi-annual review of the onboarding process, utilizing our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Feedback is collected through structured interviews with new hires, focusing on security awareness. This aligns with our ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that we maintain a high level of security consciousness among employees. Customer responsibility for security training is clearly defined in our service agreements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How frequently are the hardening practices for corporate devices reviewed and updated to address emerging security threats or vulnerabilities?\nA: Kestrel Cloud reviews its hardening practices quarterly. This aligns with our compliance program, which adheres to industry standards such as ISO 27001 and NIST. Our security team is responsible for implementing updates based on identified vulnerabilities. Customers are encouraged to follow their own security protocols in conjunction with our guidelines."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: In the event of a security incident, what are the defined timelines for notifying affected customers, and how does your organization ensure compliance with these timelines?\nA: Kestrel Cloud notifies affected customers of security incidents within 48 hours, as outlined in our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Our incident response team follows strict protocols to ensure timely communication, and we leverage automated alert systems to facilitate this process. Adherence to these timelines is governed by internal controls and regular compliance checks against our established standards."}
