{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What procedures are in place to manage the expiry of policies, including how stakeholders are notified and what actions are taken upon expiry?\nA: Kestrel Cloud adheres to a strict compliance program that mandates policy reviews every six months. Notifications are sent out automatically through our compliance management system, ensuring timely alerts to stakeholders. Upon expiry, policies are archived, and relevant teams initiate a review process to determine if updates are necessary, in accordance with ISO 27001 standards. This systematic approach ensures ongoing compliance and operational integrity."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How does your organization handle exceptions to standard access control policies, and what approval process is followed?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows a strict compliance program for handling access control exceptions. Any deviation from standard policies requires documented approval from a designated Compliance Officer. This process is in line with our ISO 27001 framework. Requests are logged and tracked for audit purposes, ensuring accountability and traceability. We emphasize the importance of adhering to these controls to maintain the security posture of Kestrel Cloud."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you document and review incidents of security policy violations to ensure that disciplinary actions are consistent and fair?\nA: Kestrel Cloud maintains a strict protocol for documenting security policy violations, referencing our Compliance Framework. Incidents are logged immediately, and reviews occur bi-monthly. Disciplinary actions are aligned with our internal standards, ensuring uniformity. We leverage our incident response tools to facilitate this process, ensuring that all actions are traceable and compliant with our established guidelines."}
