onfigurations. It also mandates biannual reviews of responsibilities to ensure stakeholder awareness of security governance roles and dictates the approval process for changes to the control framework. The program involves the evaluation of Kestrel Cloud's control framework and includes regular assessments against established standards like ISO 27001. The Compliance Program also dictates the necessity of updating the risk register, prioritizes risks aligning with industry standards such as ISO 27001, and is a strict method employed by Kestrel Cloud to categorize incidents. Kestrel Cloud's documentation, including incident reports and corrective action plans, is integral to this program, specifically aligning with ISO 27001 standards. It is a strict program followed by Kestrel Cloud that includes post-incident reviews and mandates annual reviews of incident response plans. The program also involves the bi-annual review of metrics such as incident response time and detection accuracy, and biannual tests of alerting mechanisms are conducted under its guidelines. The Compliance Program is also a system employed by Kestrel Cloud that outlines disciplinary actions for security protocol violations and is referenced by Kestrel Cloud to determine background check requirements. It mandates annual reviews of all policy documents and policy reviews every six months, and is a structured approach used by Kestrel Cloud to ensure awareness of policy exceptions, mandating biannual reviews and updates. Kestrel Cloud employs this rigorous compliance program to include regular testing of site-loss response protocols, evaluate disaster scenarios, and assess communication effectiveness during disaster recovery, which includes the Disaster Recovery Communication Standards. It also outlines the procedures and standards for compliance, including the approval of failover test results.\n\nFurthermore, the Compliance Program is leveraged by Kestrel Cloud to stay informed about emerging threats