{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What strategies does your organization implement to facilitate federated identity management across different platforms and services?\nA: Kestrel Cloud enforces federated identity management through our compliance program, which adheres to ISO 27001 and NIST standards. Clients are responsible for their identity providers, while we ensure our infrastructure supports SAML and OpenID Connect for secure authentication. Our approach is streamlined for efficiency and security, focusing on clear delineation of responsibilities. Regular reviews of access logs are conducted to maintain compliance."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What types of log sources are utilized within your environment to capture security-related events, and how are these sources prioritized for monitoring?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs system logs, application logs, and security event logs as part of our compliance program. These logs are monitored according to our established control framework, with security event logs receiving the highest priority. Compliance with ISO 27001 standards guides our monitoring processes. Customers are responsible for configuring their logging settings to ensure optimal visibility into their environments."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the approval workflow for new policies, including who is involved at each stage and how final approval is documented?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a streamlined policy approval workflow, where the compliance team drafts policies that are reviewed by the governance board. Final approval is granted by the Chief Compliance Officer, with documentation maintained in our Compliance Management System. This process adheres to ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that all policies meet rigorous compliance requirements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure the integrity of logs once they are generated, and what specific mechanisms are in place to prevent unauthorized alterations?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a comprehensive logging strategy that includes immutable log storage and strict access controls per our compliance program. We utilize tools like AWS CloudTrail and Azure Monitor to ensure logs are generated in a manner that prevents unauthorized alterations. Logs are retained for a minimum of 90 days, and any access is logged and monitored to ensure compliance with our internal policies. Customers must manage their own log access but can rely on our infrastructure to maintain log integrity."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe your log retention policy, including the duration for which logs are stored and the rationale behind this timeframe?\nA: Kestrel Cloud retains logs for a period of 90 days, in accordance with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. This timeframe is designed to facilitate rapid incident response while minimizing data retention risks. Customers are responsible for their own log management beyond this period, as outlined in our service agreements. We adhere to ISO 27001 standards, ensuring that our logging practices meet rigorous security requirements."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What role does your Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) system play in your overall logging and monitoring strategy, and how is it configured?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs a SIEM system that aligns with our compliance program, specifically the Kestrel Compliance Framework. The SIEM is configured to collect and analyze logs from all infrastructure components, ensuring we meet industry standards for security monitoring. Our customers are responsible for their own application-level logging, while we handle infrastructure security. We perform monthly audits to verify the effectiveness of our logging and monitoring processes."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: What mechanisms are in place to monitor and log traffic at the perimeter of your network to detect unauthorized access attempts?\nA: Kestrel Cloud integrates perimeter security measures with our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. We utilize automated logging mechanisms that capture all incoming and outgoing traffic for analysis. Our monitoring tools, aligned with ISO 27001 standards, provide real-time alerts for unauthorized access attempts. Customers are required to maintain their own security configurations while we oversee the infrastructure's integrity. Logs are reviewed bi-weekly to ensure compliance and security."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Can you describe the retention periods established for various categories of data within your organization?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict compliance protocols. Data retention is categorized as follows: operational logs for 12 months, customer data for 36 months, and backup data for 90 days. These intervals are aligned with our Kestrel Compliance Framework. Customers are responsible for defining their own data retention policies within these parameters, and we provide the necessary controls to facilitate this."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How often is the customer-visible telemetry reviewed for accuracy and relevance, and who is responsible for this oversight?\nA: Kestrel Cloud conducts a biannual review of customer-visible telemetry for accuracy, adhering to our compliance program standards. This process is managed by our Compliance and Risk Management team, ensuring that all telemetry aligns with established benchmarks. Customers are responsible for monitoring their own usage metrics, while we maintain the integrity of the data provided through our platform."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you ensure that your logging practices comply with relevant regulatory requirements, and what steps are taken to maintain this compliance?\nA: Kestrel Cloud follows strict compliance protocols as outlined in our Kestrel Compliance Framework. Our logging practices are aligned with NIST SP 800-53 standards, ensuring that all logs are generated, stored, and reviewed in accordance with regulatory requirements. We implement automated monitoring tools that facilitate real-time compliance checks. Customers are responsible for configuring their own logging settings, while we ensure the underlying infrastructure meets compliance mandates."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: How do you manage and log access to sensitive areas within your data centers, and what audits are conducted to review this access?\nA: Kestrel Cloud employs strict access controls to sensitive areas, with logging managed through our compliance program, Kestrel Secure. Access logs are reviewed bi-annually, ensuring adherence to industry standards. We leverage automated tools for real-time monitoring and audits, which are integral to our compliance framework. Customers are responsible for managing their own access within the cloud environment, while we maintain oversight of physical data center entry."}
{"reference_id": "", "content": "Q: Who is responsible for approving changes to your logging and monitoring policies, and what is the process for implementing these changes?\nA: Kestrel Cloud mandates that the Compliance Team approves changes to logging and monitoring policies. Our compliance program, Kestrel Secure, outlines the review process, which is conducted biannually. All changes are logged in our compliance management system, ensuring traceability and adherence to industry standards such as ISO 27001. Customers are responsible for configuring their own logging settings within the Kestrel Cloud platform."}
