{"entity": "Compliance Team", "type": "organization", "description": "The Compliance Team at Orrery Software, also known as a team within the Orrery Business Suite, is a multifaceted group primarily responsible for ensuring adherence to a wide range of policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements. This team's responsibilities encompass several critical areas, including identity management, audit processes, configuration management, data handling, regulatory compliance, risk assessment, security, and feedback review.\n\nIn terms of identity management, the Compliance Team conducts biannual reviews of practices and user access rights documentation. They are central to the audit process, which involves reviewing audit findings, collecting, documenting, and categorizing audit evidence, and reviewing formal reports. The team also prepares comprehensive action plans to address identified audit findings and is responsible for reviewing and documenting the remediation process. Their duties extend to supporting configuration management by ensuring alignment with established policies and service agreements, and by receiving logs and reports of deviations from the configuration baseline.\n\nRegarding data handling, the Compliance Team annually reviews encryption practices, including internal audits and third-party assessments, and oversees the key destruction process. They conduct thorough assessments of data types within applications, ensure adherence to GDPR and other relevant standards for subject rights requests, and are responsible for reviewing data subject requests within 45 days to identify relevant data. The team also regularly audits data retention and deletion practices, collaborates with engineering to update policies, and conducts periodic reviews of collected data.\n\nFurthermore, the Compliance Team engages in monthly reviews of regulatory changes to ensure policies remain current. They are responsible for reviewing documented risk assessments and vulnerability scans. The team leads investigations into security protocol violations, assessing their context and severity, and conducts thorough reviews of security policy violations every six months. They also review offboarding instances monthly to ensure adherence to established policies and regulatory requirements. Additionally, the Compliance Team reviews insights gathered from feedback mechanisms, reviews exceptions bi-annually, and is responsible for reviewing simulated site-loss exercises to ensure alignment with documented policies and relevant regulations. The team also oversees assessments of environmental monitoring systems. While the team is responsible for drafting new policies at Orrery Software, it also includes policy analysts and legal advisors.<SEP>The compliance team is an internal group within Orrery Software responsible for reviewing comprehensive reports and ensuring alignment with internal policies and industry standards.<SEP>A team within Orrery Software that assesses regulatory changes during the review process of vendor management policies.<SEP>A team responsible for conducting thorough reviews of non-compliance situations, documenting findings, and engaging with subprocessors for rectification."}
