{"entity": "Policies", "type": "concept", "description": "Policies are established guidelines and rules that govern various operational and security protocols within Orrery Software and Orrery Business Suite. These comprehensive guidelines are designed to ensure responsible management of access rights, emphasizing least privilege access and regular audits, as detailed in document OS-ACC-04. They mandate that all configurations align with these established guidelines and dictate the communication of audit findings. Policies also require annual training sessions for relevant staff at Orrery Business Suite.\n\nFurthermore, Policies encompass documents detailing Orrery Software's encryption methods, best practices, and rules regarding data residency. These guidelines are structured to align with COBIT and ISO standards, providing a robust approach to risk management. They also dictate shared security responsibilities between the organization and its clients.\n\nPolicies are clear guidelines established by senior management to promote compliance and risk awareness. They dictate the use of advanced Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) tools, continuous monitoring protocols, and regular security audits within Orrery Software's incident detection framework. These guidelines also govern Orrery Software's incident triage process and dictate how its network segmentation practices are reviewed and updated. Adherence to these policies is verified by an annual external audit. Policies are clearly defined and communicated to all employees and stakeholders by Orrery Software.<SEP>Documents or guidelines that are subject to annual reviews and have an expiry date, managed by Orrery Software.<SEP>Rules or principles that guide the operations of Orrery Business Suite.<SEP>Policies are established guidelines within Orrery Business Suite that are subject to exceptions and require employee awareness.<SEP>Policies are guidelines or rules that are reviewed annually, updated, and