{"entity": "Customers", "type": "organization", "description": "Customers are defined as individuals or organizations that utilize Orrery Software's services and applications, specifically within the Orrery Business Suite. They are central to a shared responsibility model, where they manage their own user accounts, ensuring access is granted only to authorized personnel and adhering to their own user access policies. This includes actively engaging in their own security practices, particularly concerning data management within their software environments. They are also recipients of comprehensive reports and insights derived from telemetry data, and are encouraged to provide feedback on it.\n\nOrrery Software provides customers with guidelines for securely managing their API keys and emphasizes their responsibilities in securing sensitive data. Customers are mandated to stay informed about library updates and potential vulnerabilities, and are responsible for ensuring compatibility with existing configurations. They are also encouraged to familiarize themselves with Orrery Software's policies to understand their responsibilities in data handling. During the onboarding process, customers are informed of their responsibilities in data encryption and key management and are provided with detailed guidelines. They are expected to implement their own access controls and are provided with tools and documentation to support compliance with industry standards. Customers are also advised to implement their own encryption strategies to complement Orrery Business Suite's offerings, and are responsible for managing their own encryption keys and defining their own key usage policies, utilizing secure configurations on their side. They are empowered to maintain oversight of their own data access and are responsible for ensuring their data classifications align with Orrery Business Suite's policies. They are encouraged to implement their own security protocols for their data within